From noah.greifer-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org  Thu Apr 25 18:22:54 2019
From: noah.greifer-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org (Noah Greifer)
Date: Thu, 25 Apr 2019 14:22:54 -0400
Subject: Re: [Question for help] Get pscore for unmatched data
In-Reply-To: <3e8bacf0.527.16a5588cb0a.Coremail.bigstar863-9Onoh4P/yGk@public.gmane.org>
References: <3e8bacf0.527.16a5588cb0a.Coremail.bigstar863@163.com>
Message-ID: <CAPhhD8=8ebD2pFw8iBen_QcMbdPiRO58rhTTtGNhYG0ZcFuhaA@mail.gmail.com>

It's stored in the "distance" entry of the matchit output object.

m.out <- matchit(A ~ X1 + X2, ...)
m.out$distance

Note that this value corresponds to the argument to distance in the call to
matchit. The default is "logit", the propensity score from a logistic
regression.

Noah

